Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 01:40:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: PS5: a write-watch fault records the 4 KiB page written.

A first write to a write-watched page cleared the watch on its whole 16 KiB host page, so GetWriteWatch reported four
pages for one store, and eight for two (kernel32 virtual.c:1750-2350, both builds, 2026-10-25). The fault now clears
only the 4 KiB page written. Its host page stays read-only while the other pages are watched (patch 1122's rule), and
the store runs through the 4 KiB path that follows (patch 1134's MMU, or a single step); each other page is recorded
at its own first write. A superset is safe for a garbage collector, which then scans more; the exact count costs up
to four faults per host page and MMU runs for writes beside watched pages.
---
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -6273,7 +6273,15 @@
             }
             else
             {
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+                /* Only the 4 KiB page written is: GetWriteWatch reported all four pages of a 16 KiB host page after one
+                 * store (kernel32 virtual.c:1750-2350, both builds, 2026-10-25). Its host page stays read-only while
+                 * its other pages are still watched, and the write runs through the 4 KiB path below (the MMU or a
+                 * step); each other page is recorded at its own first write. */
+                set_page_vprot_bits( ROUND_ADDR( addr, page_mask ), page_mask + 1, 0, VPROT_WRITEWATCH );
+#else
                 set_page_vprot_bits( page, host_page_size, 0, VPROT_WRITEWATCH );
+#endif
                 mprotect_range( page, host_page_size, 0, 0 );
             }
         }
